  "body": "**Stacked on #576** (#571), which is on #566 (#561). It includes their commits until they merge.\n\n## What changed\nLocate (#561) already warns when the part or its stock would sink into a fixture. A plain Model-page move or turn didn't check at all (#582).\n- **Shared check:** locate's sampled test and its by-name part and stock messages moved into a new `fixture_clash.rs`. `fixture_locate` calls it, and its wording is unchanged.\n- **`MoveModel::new` now carries a `warning()`:**\n  - the moved part is checked against every fixture in every setup, read through each setup's alignment;\n  - a stock that follows the move is checked only in the setup that owns it;\n  - setups with no fixtures are skipped without reading any geometry.\n- **No double check in locate:** `MoveModel::locating` and the new `MoveFixture::locating` skip it, because locate runs its own check.\n- **Fixture moves warn too:** `MoveFixture::new` checks the moved fixture against the setup's parts and stock.\n- **Where it shows:** the status line reads `moved X - warning: …` (a shared `with_warning`), and MCP `move_fixture` gains a `\"warning\"` field.\n- **A warning, not a refusal.** It warns on the result, so a part already inside a closed vise warns on every nudge.\n- **Decision record:** `docs/decisions/582-move-interpenetration.md`.\n\n## How tested\n- **New `move_interpenetration` (7):**\n  - sinking into the floor warns by name;\n  - a turn swinging into the jaw warns;\n  - a stock-only sink warns for the stock alone;\n  - a clear move warns nothing;\n  - no fixtures means no check;\n  - undo and redo of a warned move;\n  - moving the fixture into the part warns.\n- **UI:** `a_model_page_move_into_the_fixture_warns_on_the_status_line`.\n- **Gate:** move_model_stock, commands_undo, fixture_locate(_stock), fixtures, fixture_ux, setup_align, project_roundtrip, mcp_setup and the ui fixture_ux/locate tests pass. Clippy is clean.\n\nChangelog: A Model-page move or turn (and a Fixtures-page fixture move) warns by name when the part or its stock would sink into a fixture, as locate does - a warning, not a refusal (#582)\n\nFixes #582\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
